---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Blind Data: A Chart Competition | tcplot: Data Visualization in Minneapolis and St. Paul"
    description="One never-before-seen dataset, seventy-five minutes, any tools you want. Build a visualization, present it in sixty seconds, and vote."
>
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-8 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
                Upcoming: Blind Data — A Chart Competition
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, Sep 26 · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CDT
                </p>
                <p class="flex items-start gap-2 mt-1">
                    <svg
                        class="w-5 h-5 mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-gray-400"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                        fill="currentColor"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                    >
                        <path
                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                            d="M12 2c-3.866 0-7 3.07-7 6.857 0 4.34 4.686 9.86 6.412 11.74a.8.8 0 0 0 1.176 0C14.314 18.717 19 13.197 19 8.857 19 5.07 15.866 2 12 2Zm0 9.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 0-5 2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0 5Z"
                            clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                    </svg>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >The Coffee Shop NE</span
                        ><br />2852 Johnson St NE · Minneapolis, MN</span
                    >
                </p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                One dataset. Seventy-five minutes. May the best chart win.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Join <span class="font-silkscreen">tcplot</span> for Blind
                Data, our first chart competition — blind because nobody sees
                the dataset until the clock starts. Everyone gets the same
                never-before-seen data at
                the same moment, a hard time limit, and total freedom of tools —
                D3 or ggplot2, Tableau or Excel, Claude Code or colored pencils.
                When time is called, every chart goes up, everyone presents for
                sixty seconds, and the room votes.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                The same table of numbers contains many different charts — a
                distribution, a trend, an outlier, a joke — and which one you
                find says as much about you as about the data. Working under a
                clock against twenty other people is the fastest way we know to
                see how wide the design space really is.
            </p>

            <div class="flex justify-center mt-12 mb-8">
                <div class="max-w-2xl w-full rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                    <img
                        src="/images/blind-data-colorful-worksheet.png"
                        alt="A classic Macintosh spreadsheet titled Worksheet1 with every cell filled in a different bright color"
                        class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                How the event will flow
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-8">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Rules &amp; setup (15 min).</span
                        > Intros, form solo entries or pairs, get your machines and
                        tools ready. The dataset stays sealed until the clock
                        starts — nobody, including the organizers' friends, sees
                        it early.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Dataset reveal.</span
                        > A link goes up on the screen: one clean CSV, small
                        enough to open anywhere, rich enough to support a dozen
                        different stories. A short data dictionary is included —
                        the challenge is design, not decoding.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Build sprint (75 min).</span
                        > Make the best visualization you can. Any tool, any
                        medium, any level of interactivity — the only
                        requirements are that it uses the event dataset and can
                        be shown to the room.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Pencils down &amp; gallery walk.</span
                        > Everything goes up — screens, projector, paper taped to
                        the wall. Wander, look closely, ask questions.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Lightning presentations.</span
                        > Sixty seconds each: what you found, what you encoded,
                        and one decision you'd defend. The clock is merciless
                        and that's the fun of it.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Vote &amp; awards.</span
                        > Ballots, tallies, and a chart of the votes — because
                        of course the results get visualized too.</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                The categories
            </h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                You can't win them all — one entry, one prize, so the glory
                spreads:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-8">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Clearest.</span
                        > A stranger understands it in ten seconds, unaided.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Most beautiful.</span
                        > The one people photograph.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Most surprising.</span
                        > Found something in the data nobody else found, or a
                        form nobody else tried.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >Best human–AI duet.</span
                        > For entries built with an agent: the sharpest example
                        of a person steering and a model executing.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        ><span class="font-semibold text-gray-900"
                            >People's choice.</span
                        > The catch-all crown.</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                The rules
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-8">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        >Any tool is legal, and AI assistants are explicitly
                        welcome — Claude Code, notebooks, whatever you drive
                        best. The room will notice the difference between
                        steering an agent well and pasting its first draft.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        >Solo or pairs. Pairs present together and split the
                        glory.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        >The event dataset must be the star. Bringing in a
                        second dataset to join against it is allowed — and has
                        won chartathons before.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        >When time is called, hands off. Unfinished is a
                        legitimate aesthetic.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">&#x25B8;</span>
                    <span
                        >You can't vote for your own entry. You knew that.</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                What to bring
            </h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                A laptop with your weapon of choice installed and working —
                seventy-five minutes is too short to fight an environment. Or
                bring nothing and go analog; we'll have paper, markers, and
                supplies on hand. If you plan to use an AI tool, log in before
                the clock starts.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                Who this is for
            </h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Everyone from first-chart beginners to people with strong
                opinions about axis label rotation. The time limit is a great
                equalizer: nobody's polish survives seventy-five minutes, so
                what wins is ideas. Competitive in format, friendly in fact.
            </p>

            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Hope to see you there!
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
